  "observations": [
    "The accepted compiler's refusal is raised at cfrontend/TypedScalarFrontend.ml line 398 of its build tree /root/build/lane-backend-accept-20260925/compiler-final (sha256 da7352969a24a1e24d1ddbf77d9c2e76b28d49a69a394fdd450398a6b198667a, 35679 bytes), which refuses every Clight Sswitch.",
    "The normalized control program has no conditional and compiles through the accepted typed route (ccomp exit 0, 52496 assembly lines) with every erased position and five retained 64-bit member alignments; compiler-diff then refuses its image at layout because 242568 bytes of text exceed the 32768-byte window between 0x80000000 and the data section at 0x80008000. No target run or comparison verdict exists for it.",
    "The control driver agrees with the generator's expected answers natively on all 640 seeded rows under UBSan; its perturbed driver fails natively (exit 1) and meets the same layout refusal on target.",
    "The perturbed probe fails natively (exit 1) and meets the same switch refusal on target, so its target leg is a refusal rather than a failing comparison verdict.",
    "Velus warns that it could not check semantic existence (construction not supported) for the control program; the start/restart node compiles with an empty log.",
    "Check 5 is not reached because check 4 failed; a post-verdict rehash found all 27 frozen inputs and 10 tool identities unchanged."
  ],
